# SQAuto Deployment & Bug Fixes

I have implemented the fixes for the "502 Bad Gateway" error and the React component crash at line 62.

## Changes Overview

### 1. Fixed `ExportPanel` Prop Mismatch
The `ExportPanel` component was not accepting the `disabled` prop being passed to it. This would cause a build or runtime error. I have updated it to accept and use this prop.

```tsx
// apps/web/src/components/ExportPanel.tsx
interface ExportPanelProps {
  disabled?: boolean;
}

export default function ExportPanel({ disabled }: ExportPanelProps) {
  // ... usage of disabled prop ...
}
```

### 2. Improved Nginx Config for Cloudflare
I updated `scripts/setup_nginx.sh` to include essential proxy headers for Cloudflare and modern Next.js deployments. This ensures the original IP and protocol are correctly passed to the application.

```nginx
proxy_set_header X-Real-IP \$remote_addr;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For \$proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto \$scheme;
```

### 3. Production Environment Configuration
Updated `.env` to point to the correct production domain for the API.

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://sqauto.zeraynce.com/api
```

## Next Steps: Applying to Server

Since you have already pushed to GitHub, please follow these steps on your server at `4.230.17.169`:

1.  **Pull the latest code**:
    ```bash
    git pull origin main
    ```

2.  **Update Nginx**:
    ```bash
    bash scripts/setup_nginx.sh
    ```

3.  **Restart & Rebuild Containers**:
    This will ensure the new code and `.env` settings are applied inside Docker.
    ```bash
    docker-compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml down
    docker-compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml up -d --build
    ```

4.  **SSL Verification**:
    Ensure you have run Certbot if you haven't already:
    ```bash
    sudo certbot --nginx -d sqauto.zeraynce.com
    ```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> If you still see a "Bad Gateway", check your container logs with `docker logs sqauto_web` to see if there are any runtime errors during startup.
